//! Accounts: sign up, log in, log out, password reset by email, and the
//! [`CurrentUser`] extractor.
//!
//! Passwords are hashed with Argon2id; sessions live in the database (table
//! `zapline_sessions`) behind a signed cookie, keyed by `SESSION_SECRET`
//! (debug builds fall back to a development key). Protect a handler by
//! taking `CurrentUser` (401 when logged out), or `Option<CurrentUser>` to
//! treat visitors differently.
//!
//! Reset links are emailed through `SMTP_URL` and point at `APP_URL`. While
//! developing, without `SMTP_URL`, they appear at <http://localhost:8080/_dev/mail>.
//!
//! Users can turn on two-factor login (an authenticator app, plus one-time
//! recovery codes) and sign in with a link emailed to them. Every way of
//! signing in (password, link, reset, GitHub/Google) asks for the second
//! factor when it is on.
//!
//! "Continue with GitHub / Google" turns on when `GITHUB_CLIENT_ID` and
//! `GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET` (or the `GOOGLE_` pair) are set. The callback URL
//! to register there is `{APP_URL}/auth/github/callback`.
//!
//! The admin panel at `/admin` lets in only the accounts listed in
//! `ADMIN_EMAILS` (comma-separated), in every build, once their owner has
//! proved the address: by a password reset link, or by logging in with
//! GitHub/Google. Anyone can sign up with any address, so the address alone
//! proves nothing.

